\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The CAT workspace, mid-conversation. Channels, agents and people are listed in the sidebar, the last grouped by discipline; the button beside the mark switches between light and dark. The agent answers \emph  {a particular reader}---it opens with the reader's name, because it was told who asked and what they work on---and writes the wind field in the notation of the discipline rather than in prose, which the browser renders from the \LaTeX  {} the model produced. The grey line beneath a reply records which model answered, what it cost, and who asked for it.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:interface}{{1}{3}{The CAT workspace, mid-conversation. Channels, agents and people are listed in the sidebar, the last grouped by discipline; the button beside the mark switches between light and dark. The agent answers \emph {a particular reader}---it opens with the reader's name, because it was told who asked and what they work on---and writes the wind field in the notation of the discipline rather than in prose, which the browser renders from the \LaTeX {} the model produced. The grey line beneath a reply records which model answered, what it cost, and who asked for it}{figure.1}{}}
